FE-3237 negative control — the /useOrder record draws Pay now on a payable order.

Target spec:  tests/e2e/orders.spec.ts
Target case:  "Pay now shows on a payable order and opens the pay overlay"
Mutation:     inverts the `canPay` gate on the Pay now header action in
              order.presentation.ts — `gate: "canPay"` becomes `gate: "!canPay"`.
              The record surface reads the `!` prefix as negation
              (RecordSurface.vue isGateOpen), so on a payable order the gate now
              closes and the Pay now action is not drawn.
Why RED:      the recorded order is payable (canPay true), so the paired case
              asserts Pay now is visible and the pay overlay opens. With the gate
              inverted the action is hidden, so the visibility assertion fails.
Why the rest stay GREEN: no other case reads the Pay now action — the other
              record case draws the order whole, the single-read case counts the
              load read, and the five collection cases never reach the record.
Authored by:  developer seat (mutant only), anchored to d21241a5b. The prover
              applies it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to
              construct it.

